<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"> <head> <meta charset="utf-8"> <meta content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, user-scalable=yes" name="viewport"> <title>text_styles</title> </head> <body> <main> <h1 id="sec:styles">1 Emphasis and revision styles</h1> <p>Plain text surrounds <em>emphasized words</em> and <strong>bold words</strong>. Nested emphasis combines <em>an emphasized phrase with <strong>bold content</strong>
</em>.</p> <p>The result includes <span data-custom-style="Revision Char">newly revised wording</span>.</p> <figure id="fig:original"> <img alt="Figure 1 Original figure caption." src="figure.svg"> <figcaption aria-hidden="true">Figure 1 Original figure caption.</figcaption> </figure> <figure id="fig:revised"> <img alt="Figure 2 Revised figure caption with updated details." src="figure.svg"> <figcaption aria-hidden="true">Figure 2 <span data-custom-style="Revision Char">Revised figure caption with updated details.</span>
</figcaption> </figure> <p>Both Figure <a href="#fig:original">1</a> and Figure <a href="#fig:revised">2</a> remain available as numbered references.</p> <p>A paragraph containing only inline math must keep its inline equation form:</p> <p>
<span class="inline math">x_i</span>
</p> <p>Ordinary prose with inline math <span class="inline math">y_i</span> follows as a control.</p> </main> </body> </html>
